# Trivy IaC scan exceptions. This is a disposable FinOps demo torn down with
# `terraform destroy`, so several production-only controls are intentionally
# disabled. Each ignore below has its rationale.

# Public static demo site — mutual-TLS client certificates would block normal access.
AVD-AZU-0001

# Static site doesn't authenticate to downstream services, so no managed identity.
AVD-AZU-0002

# Demo content is intentionally public (no auth backend).
AVD-AZU-0003

# Restricting Key Vault network access would lock out `az` CLI / Terraform data plane.
AVD-AZU-0013

# Purge protection is irreversible; left off so `terraform destroy` can clean up.
AVD-AZU-0016

# Restricting storage network would break the daily Cost Management export.
AVD-AZU-0012

# Storage analytics logging is out of scope (see Azure Monitor diagnostic settings).
AVD-AZU-0057

# LRS is a deliberate cost choice (FinOps); GRS would double the cost of a demo.
AVD-AZU-0058

# Customer-managed keys are overkill for a demo cost-export container.
AVD-AZU-0060

# Infrastructure double-encryption is overkill and not available in every region.
AVD-AZU-0061
